		<title>How to be unemployed: Glenn Kelman on life after Redfin</title>
		<link>https://www.geekwire.com/2026/how-to-be-unemployed-glenn-kelman-on-life-after-redfin/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:47:53 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Glenn Kelman]]></dc:creator>
						<category><![CDATA[Real Estate]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Startups]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Glenn Kelman]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Redfin]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.geekwire.com/?p=963905</guid>
				<description><![CDATA[<img width="1200" height="489" src="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Green beaded leather bracelet spelling out the word Enough" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet.jpg 1200w, https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet-768x313.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px"><br>Glenn Kelman, who led Redfin as CEO for 20 years, writes about the 10 months of unemployment that came before co-founding a new AI-native company. He considered becoming a high school teacher, a bagel shopkeeper and a state legislative candidate, and used AI to test ideas with potential co-founders. <a href="https://www.geekwire.com/2026/how-to-be-unemployed-glenn-kelman-on-life-after-redfin/">Read More</a>]]></description>
								<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="489" src="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet.jpg" alt="Green beaded leather bracelet spelling out the word Enough" class="wp-image-963904" srcset="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet.jpg 1200w, https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/glenn-kelman-enough-bracelet-768x313.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">At a conference, a fashion entrepreneur gave Glenn Kelman a bracelet that said “we are enough.” (Image via Glenn Kelman)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After 20 years at Redfin, and 10 months of unemployment, I’ve co-founded a new company. My business partner and I will announce our plans after we’ve built our product, but in the meantime GeekWire asked me to explain what I learned in the transition between Redfin and this new venture.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Many of us are in transition because society is in transition, with AI hollowing out big companies and making it easier to start new companies.</p>]]></content:encoded>
							<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">963905</post-id>	</item>
