		<category><![CDATA[Funding]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[powerlattice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[semiconductor]]></category>

		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.geekwire.com/?p=961939</guid>
				<description><![CDATA[<img width="1260" height="840" src="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice.jpg 1260w, https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice-768x512.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1260px) 100vw, 1260px"><br>The new funding nearly triples what the Vancouver, Wash.-based semiconductor startup had raised when it came out of stealth last year. Powerlattice says its tech can cut AI chip energy use by more than half. <a href="https://www.geekwire.com/2026/filing-chip-startup-powerlattice-raises-86m-to-ease-ais-power-crunch/">Read More</a>]]></description>
								<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1260" height="840" src="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-961945" srcset="https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice.jpg 1260w, https://cdn.geekwire.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/powerlattice-768x512.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1260px) 100vw, 1260px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Powerlattice founders, from left: Gang Ren, Peng Zou, and Sujith Dermal. (Powerlattice / Walden Kirsch Photo)</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.powerlatticeinc.com/">Powerlattice</a>, a Vancouver, Wash.-based startup developing chips that cut the power demands of AI processors, has raised $86 million, according to an <a href="https://secgems.com/s/0002069744-26-000002.nc?sr=k">SEC filing</a> on Friday.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The new funding is nearly triple the $31 million the company had raised when it emerged from stealth last November with a <a href="https://www.geekwire.com/2025/powerlattice-a-new-semiconductor-startup-backed-by-former-intel-ceo-raises-25m/">]]></content:encoded>
